até
ate
# "até ao"/"até à": "até" (until) stacked with the contracted article "ao"/"à"
# ("do dia 3 ... até ao dia 5") -- the split scanner finds the bare "até"
# first (it precedes "ao" in the sentence), so without the two-word surface
# registered the trailing "ao" was left an unclaimed token, stranded in the
# composed range's remainder.  Registered longest-first (see
# ``_conn_surfaces``) so it is tried before the bare "até" and swallows both
# words when they actually appear together; a bare "até o dia" (no
# contraction) is untouched, and "até" alone still matches when "ao"/"à"
# does not follow.
até ao
até à
